 "_doc": "Seafloor around the offshore reef (05/11, Sergio: rocks, sharks, algae and sea life; MareReefWorld.cpp). Each 'dressing' entry scatters instances (one HISM per mesh, drawn on the GPU, culled past cull_cm) around every reef cluster centre (clusters: x,y cm; the reef lies ~9 m deep): count per cluster plus 'extra' spread over the whole reef strip, uniform scale in [scale], sunk 'sink' cm into the sand, yaw random, 'tilt' degrees of random lean. A spot is kept only where a sphere of 'clear' cm radius dropped from above reaches the sand (floor_below cm or deeper) without touching coral or another rock. 'shadow' casts dynamic shadows. Sharks: blacktip reef sharks circling their cluster at depth, slowly, turning away from swimmers closer than 'shy' cm. Models: tools/ue58/gen_seafloor.py (Sea_*), rocks and shells from Poly Haven (CC0, already in the project).",
