  "_doc": "05/11 (Sergio: 'faça um gerador com rochas, corais e algas marinhas, preencha todo fundo'; 'fundo precisa ser bem fundo, uns 100m'). The whole sea floor in front of the island gets dressed by depth (MareReefWorld::FillFloor), cell by cell over x and y (cm). profile: floor height z along y after the beach terrain ends (terrain_until; up to there a trace finds the terrain): the ramp to the reef shelf at -9 m, the shelf, the drop-off and the deep floor at -100 m. mare_water.ensure_seabed builds the sand planes on the same profile. Each kind: density per 100 m2 where the floor z is inside 'depth' [lowest, highest], uniform scale in [scale], sunk 'sink' cm (x scale), random lean 'tilt' degrees, 'align' 0..1 to the slope, optional 'patch' (noise size, cm) keeping only the patches above patch_cut, culled past 'cull' cm. The reef strip itself (dressing above) is skipped, plus reef_pad cm.",
